DFS detects a cycle if it encounters an already visited vertex that is not the direct parent of the current vertex. The crucial additional parameter is the `parent` of the current node in the DFS tree.
```python
def dfs_undirected_cycle(u, parent, visited, adj):
    visited[u] = True
    for v in adj[u]:
        if not visited[v]:
            if dfs_undirected_cycle(v, u, visited, adj):
                return True
        elif v != parent: # v is visited and not parent
            return True # Cycle detected
    return False
```
